Subject: [PATCH] drm: bridge: lt9611: test settling before crystal selection

Temporary DT510 diagnostic, not a production timing requirement. Build 693
avoids the startup failure by retaining the ring clock. Test whether an
additional 1000 ms on the ring clock before selecting the crystal permits
startup with the reference clock used by upstream and vendor code.

Apply after 0039 INSTEAD OF the ring-clock diagnostic 0040. The existing
0x8101=0x18 write and all other setup values remain unchanged. Wait once
after the already-powered guard, before the first write; retain the bounded
transport retries and STOP error reporting. Do not add a full wait per retry.

The reset path already waits 100 ms after release. An extra second is a
conservative comparison interval, not a measured or specified oscillator
startup bound. A pass supports timing sensitivity, not a defective crystal
or a validated minimum delay. Repeated cold/warm starts and timing/mode
qualification remain necessary. Do not hide errors or accept late recovery
as proof of successful first startup.

Upstream-Status: Inappropriate [temporary DT510 crystal-settling diagnostic]
Assisted-by: Briar
---
--- a/drivers/gpu/drm/bridge/lontium-lt9611.c
+++ b/drivers/gpu/drm/bridge/lontium-lt9611.c
@@ -515,6 +515,9 @@ static int lt9611_power_on(struct lt9611 *lt9611)
 	if (lt9611->power_on)
 		return 0;
 
+	/* Diagnostic only: test oscillator settling BEFORE switching clocks. */
+	msleep(1000);
+
 	/* This setup sequence is idempotent, including the crystal selection. */
 	for (attempt = 0; attempt < 3; attempt++) {
 		ret = regmap_multi_reg_write(lt9611->regmap, seq, ARRAY_SIZE(seq));
